    id: "f72a7ac5935791565a19",
    cat: "conflitti",
    title: "Hundreds from Russian-occupied Oleshky land in Belarus en route to Ukraine",
    summary: "Four planes transporting evacuees from the war-ravaged city have arrived in Belarus's Gomel.",
    preview: "Four planes transporting evacuees from the war-ravaged city have arrived in Belarus’s Gomel. Hundreds of residents from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky have been transported to Belarus, as part of a major evacuation mission under a truce that the White House says United States First Lady Melania Trump helped broker. Four planes carrying the Oleshky evacuees arrived in the southeastern Belarusian town of Gomel on Saturday, said Ukrainian parliament member David Arakhamia.",
    body: "Four planes transporting evacuees from the war-ravaged city have arrived in Belarus’s Gomel.\n\nHundreds of residents from the Russian-occupied Ukrainian town of Oleshky have been transported to Belarus, as part of a major evacuation mission under a truce that the White House says United States First Lady Melania Trump helped broker.\n\nFour planes carrying the Oleshky evacuees arrived in the southeastern Belarusian town of Gomel on Saturday, said Ukrainian parliament member David Arakhamia.\n\nRecommended Stories\n\nlist of 3 items\n\n- list 1 of 3Melania or the pope: Who brokered Russia-Ukraine ceasefire in Oleshky?\n\n- list 2 of 3Russia’s alleged sabotage campaign in Europe raises fears of escalation\n\n- list 3 of 3At least 14 people killed in attack on Ukraine train station\n\nThe group was met in Gomel by rescue workers, medical teams and Red Cross volunteers, Belarusian state media reported.\n\nFrom there, they were due to be transported to Ukrainian territory “within hours”, said Arakhamia.\n\nThe civilians from Oleshky, which has suffered from major food and medicine shortages after years of fighting, began the long journey out of their region in bus convoys on Friday, under a rare regional truce that is expected to continue through Sunday.\n\nThe estimated 2,000 residents were offered the choice of travelling to Ukrainian- or Russian-held territory, or remaining in the city with replenished food and medical supplies.\n\nRussia and Ukraine have not specified how many people chose to leave the city, but Melania Trump posted on Friday that the humanitarian convoy could safely evacuate more than 750 people.\n\nRussia’s ombudswoman and lead representative on the mission, Yana Lantratova, said buses also transported Oleshky residents who wanted to live in Russia.\n\nAside from the first lady’s apparent role, Pope Leo XIV – the first American pontiff – also pressed Russian and Ukrainian leaders to allow aid deliveries and civilian evacuations.",
    content_status: "full",
    source: "Al Jazeera",
    url: "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/31/hundreds-from-russian-occupied-oleshky-land-in-belarus-en-route-to-ukraine?traffic_source=rss",
